#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:5
msgid "AMDGPU Memory Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:11
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "簡介"

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:13
msgid ""
"The :ref:`LLVM memory model<memmodel>` provides broad guarantees that are "
"sufficient to implement inter-thread communication via memory. But in most "
"communication patterns, not all memory accesses performed by a thread need "
"to be exposed to other threads. Even when they do need to be exposed, not "
"all threads may need to observe these memory accesses. This document "
"describes the *AMDGPU memory model* that allows the user to control how the "
"side-effects of memory accesses are propagated across threads. The "
"programmer expresses this using **new intrinsics and metadata** as described "
"below, and the implementation can then choose a more efficient mechanism to "
"complete them, such as the cache policy bits in an AMDGPU device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:24
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model allows executions that are not allowed by the LLVM "
"memory model. At the same time, a simple mapping can be used to implement "
"these new intrinsics and metadata using operations defined in the default "
"LLVM memory model. Thus, **there exists a safe-by-default implementation** "
"that produces executions that are valid in both models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:31
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:36
msgid "Memory Accesses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:34
msgid ""
"Operations that read or write locations in memory are termed as *memory "
"accesses*. Typical examples are ``load``, ``store`` and atomic instructions, "
"as well as many intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:41
msgid "Synchronizing Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:39
msgid ""
"Synchronizing operations control how the side-effects of memory accesses are "
"propagated in the system. Typical examples are atomic operations (including "
"fences) with at least ``release`` or ``acquire`` ordering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:46
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:48
msgid ""
"A *scope* is an abstract description of sets of memory accesses and "
"synchronizing operations in a multi-threaded execution environment. Each "
"such set is called an *instance* of that scope, or a *scope instance* for "
"short."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:52
msgid ""
"Each memory access or synchronizing operation belongs to at most one "
"instance of every scope defined by the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:54
msgid ""
"When an operation ``X`` specifies a scope ``S``, it indicates the instance "
"of ``S`` that contains ``X``. This scope instance is also termed as *X's "
"instance of scope S*, or just *X's scope instance* when ``S`` is implied by "
"the context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:58
msgid ""
"When an operation does not specify a scope, it indicates the *system* scope "
"defined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:62
msgid "LLVM scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:64
msgid ""
"The LLVM Language Reference defines the following :ref:`scopes<syncscope>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:68
msgid "*system scope* (empty string \"\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:67
msgid ""
"There exists a single instance of this scope that contains the memory "
"accesses and synchronizing operations performed by all threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:72
msgid "\"singlethread\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:71
msgid ""
"Each thread corresponds to a \"singlethread\" scope instance that contains "
"the memory accesses and synchronizing operations performed by that thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:75
msgid "AMDGPU scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:77
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU backend further refines the LLVM scopes with the following target-"
"defined scopes and constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:80
msgid "*system scope* (same as LLVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:81
msgid "\"agent\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:82
msgid "\"cluster\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:83
msgid "\"workgroup\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:84
msgid "\"wavefront\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:85
msgid "\"singlethread\" scope (same as LLVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:87
msgid ""
"These are arranged from largest scope (*system scope*) to smallest scope "
"(\"singlethread\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:90
msgid ""
"Every instance ``X`` of some scope ``S1`` other than \"singlethread\" scope "
"is partitioned by the scope ``S2`` one level below it. Each subset defined "
"by this partition is an instance of ``S2`` and is called a *subscope "
"instance* of ``X``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:93
msgid ""
"It follows that if two scope instances ``X`` and ``Y`` intersect, then their "
"intersection is the smaller of ``X`` and ``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:95
msgid ""
"A scope ``S1`` is a *subscope* of a scope ``S2`` if every instance of ``S1`` "
"is a subscope instance of some instance of ``S2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:98
msgid ""
"**Inclusive Scopes**: Two operations ``X`` and ``Y`` are said to have "
"*inclusive scopes* if the scope instance of each operation contains the "
"other operation. In that case, the *common scope instance* ``S'`` of ``X`` "
"and ``Y`` is the intersection of their scope instances. The scope "
"corresponding to ``S'`` is also termed as the *common scope* of ``X`` and "
"``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:105
msgid "Availability and Visibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:107
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model is built on top of the :ref:`happens-"
"before<memmodel>` order defined by the LLVM memory model. But when one of "
"the new intrinsics or metadata is used, **happens-before by itself is not "
"sufficient** to describe its observable effects. Instead, the AMDGPU model "
"uses *availability* and *visibility* to describe how the side-effects of "
"these operations propagate to other threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:114
msgid ""
"Availability determines how *far* the side-effects of a write have been "
"forwarded in the system relative to that write. Visibility determines how "
"*close* the side-effects of the same write have reached relative to an "
"observer operation (typically a read)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:119
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model *does not change the structure of happens-before*, "
"but changes the rules that determine how operations may observe the side-"
"effects of other operations that *happen-before* them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:123
msgid ""
"Consider a write ``W`` that ``happens-before`` a read ``R`` to the same "
"address:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:125
msgid ""
"``R`` can potentially observe the side-effects of ``W`` **only if W is "
"visible** to ``R``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:127
msgid ""
"``W`` can potentially be visible to ``R`` **only if W is first made "
"available** to ``R``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:130
msgid ""
"The instructions used in the default LLVM memory model automatically satisfy "
"these necessary conditions, and hence they can be explained using the rules "
"from either memory model. But the new intrinsics and metadata *opt out* of "
"the LLVM memory model, and can only be explained using the AMDGPU memory "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:138
msgid "store-available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:147
msgid ""
"The ``@llvm.amdgcn.av.global.store.b128`` intrinsic performs a non-atomic "
"*store-available* operation on ``ptr`` with scope ``scope``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:150
msgid ""
"An atomic operation that results in a store operation is a *store-available* "
"operation with scope ``syncscope``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:156
msgid "load-visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:165
msgid ""
"The ``@llvm.amdgcn.av.global.load.b128`` intrinsic performs a non-atomic "
"*load-visible* operation on ``ptr`` with scope ``scope``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:168
msgid ""
"An atomic operation that results in a read operation is a *load-visible* "
"operation with scope ``syncscope``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:173
msgid ""
"Metadata cannot be used to model this using ordinary load/store operations, "
"because the scope is necessary for correctness. In a hypothetical operation "
"like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:181
msgid ""
"If the metadata is dropped or ignored, there is no guarantee that the store "
"will become available at the intended scope. In implementation terms, the "
"store may be completed at a nearer cache than the one required for that "
"scope. A corresponding *load-visible* that does not access the same near "
"cache will fail to observe this store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:190
msgid "AV Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:196
msgid ""
"The presence of this metadata removes the ability of synchronizing "
"operations to establish availability and visibility, and essentially creates "
"*non-av* synchronizing operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:200
msgid ""
"For a synchronizing operation which itself accesses memory (e.g., ``store "
"atomic release`` or ``load atomic acquire``), the metadata does not affect "
"the availability or the visibility of the access performed by the operation "
"itself. It only affects the synchronization of other memory accesses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:206
msgid "MakeAvailable and MakeVisible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:216
msgid ""
"A synchronizing operation with at least ``release`` ordering is a "
"``MakeAvailable`` operation with scope ``syncscope``, if it is not marked as "
"``!{!\"amdgcn-av\", !\"none\"}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:220
msgid ""
"A synchronizing operation with at least ``acquire`` ordering is a "
"``MakeVisible`` operation with scope ``syncscope``, if it is not marked as "
"``!{!\"amdgcn-av\", !\"none\"}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:239
msgid "Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:243
msgid ""
"**TODO:** These ordering operations affect all address spaces. We need to "
"eventually make that a parameter similar to the storage class parameter on "
"operations and orders in Vulkan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:248
msgid "Availability Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:250
msgid ""
"An operation ``X`` is an *availability operation* on a write ``W`` if one of "
"the following holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:253
msgid "``X`` is ``W`` itself, and ``W`` is a *store-available* operation, or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:254
msgid ""
"``X`` is a ``MakeAvailable`` operation that follows ``W`` in program order, "
"or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:256
msgid ""
"``X`` is a ``MakeAvailable`` operation whose scope instance includes ``W``, "
"and there is an availability operation ``Z`` on ``W`` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:259
msgid "``Z`` happens-before ``X``, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:260
msgid "``Z``'s scope instance includes ``X``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:262
msgid ""
"Then ``X`` makes ``W`` available in its own scope instance ``S`` and every "
"subscope instance of ``S`` that also includes ``W``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:266
msgid "Visibility Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:268
msgid ""
"An operation ``Y`` is a *visibility operation* on a write ``W`` if ``Y`` is "
"a *load-visible* operation to the same address, or a ``MakeVisible`` "
"operation, and one of the following holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:272
msgid ""
"There exists an *availability* operation ``X`` on write ``W`` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:274 ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:282
msgid "``X`` happens-before ``Y``, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:275
msgid "``X`` and ``Y`` specify inclusive scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:277
msgid ""
"Then ``Y`` makes ``W`` visible in the common scope instance ``S`` of ``X`` "
"and ``Y``, and every subscope instance of ``S`` that includes ``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:280
msgid "There exists a *visibility* operation ``X`` on write ``W`` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:283
msgid ""
"``X`` makes ``W`` visible in a scope instance ``S1`` that includes ``Y``, "
"and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:284
msgid "``X`` is included in the scope instance ``S2`` of ``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:286
msgid ""
"Then ``Y`` makes ``W`` visible in the intersection ``S`` of ``S1`` and "
"``S2``, and every subscope instance of ``S`` that includes ``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:290
msgid "Location Order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:292
msgid ""
"A write ``W`` is *location-ordered* before an access ``Y`` to the same "
"address if ``W`` is program-ordered before ``Y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:295
msgid ""
"A write ``W`` is *location-ordered* before a write ``W1`` to the same "
"address if there exists an availability operation ``Z`` on ``W`` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:298
msgid "``Z`` happens-before ``W1``, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:299
msgid "``W1`` is included in ``Z``'s scope instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:301
msgid ""
"A write ``W`` is *location-ordered* before a read ``R`` to the same address "
"if there exists a visibility operation ``Z`` on write ``W`` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:304
msgid "``Z`` is ``R`` itself, or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:305
msgid "``Z`` precedes ``R`` in program order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:307
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model overrides the definition of each byte in the :ref:"
"`LLVM memory model<memmodel>` as follows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:310
msgid ""
"Every (defined) read operation ``R`` reads a series of bytes written by "
"(defined) write operations. Each initialized global is assumed to have an "
"initial *system scoped* atomic write operation that is *location-ordered* "
"before any other read or write to that same location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:315
msgid ""
"For each byte of a read ``R``, ``R`` may see any write to the same byte, "
"except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:317
msgid ""
"If a write ``W1`` is *location-ordered* before a write ``W2``, and ``W2`` is "
"*location-ordered* before a read ``R``, then ``R`` may not see ``W1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:319
msgid ""
"If a read ``R`` happens-before a write ``W3``, then ``R`` may not see ``W3``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:321
msgid "The value returned by ``R`` is then defined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:323
msgid ""
"If no write is *location-ordered* before a read ``R``, then ``R`` returns "
"``undef``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:325
msgid ""
"Otherwise if the set consisting of ``R`` and all writes that ``R`` may see "
"contains only atomic operations with inclusive scopes, then ``R`` returns "
"the value written by one of those writes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:328
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if ``R`` may see some write that is not *location-ordered* before "
"``R``, then ``R`` returns ``undef``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:330
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if ``R`` may see exactly one write ``W``, then ``R`` returns the "
"value written by ``W``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:332
msgid "Otherwise, ``R`` returns ``undef``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:335
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:339
msgid "This section is informational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:341
msgid "The following properties follow from the definitions above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:343
msgid ""
"**Happens-before is necessary for location-order.** A write ``W`` is "
"*location-ordered* before a read ``R`` only if ``W`` happens-before ``R``. "
"This follows from the definition of availability and visibility operations, "
"which always require a happens-before link with the preceding operation in "
"the chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:349
msgid ""
"**A write cannot be made available in a scope that does not contain it.** "
"The definition of an availability operation ``X`` requires that ``X``'s "
"scope instance includes ``W`` as a precondition. Since every scope instance "
"that includes ``X`` also includes ``W``, availability cannot reach a scope "
"instance that excludes ``W``. In other words, availability can only \"expand "
"outwards\" into progressively larger scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:356
msgid ""
"**Visibility is bounded by availability.** When a write is available in a "
"scope instance, it can be made visible in that scope instance by a "
"visibility operation with the corresponding scope. Subsequent "
"``MakeVisible`` operations make that write visible into narrower scope "
"instances towards the observer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:361
msgid ""
"**A write can be made visible in a scope instance that does not contain it."
"** The definition of a *visibility operation* anchors scope instances to the "
"observer (``Y``), not to the original write. The only precondition is that "
"the write must already be visible or available in the scope instance of the "
"visibility operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.rst:367
msgid ""
"**Availability and visibility chains.** For a write ``W`` to be visible to a "
"read ``R`` anywhere in the system, the sufficient condition is a chain of "
"happens-before edges that include availability and visibility operations "
"with inclusive scopes. It is not necessary that ``W`` and ``R`` themselves "
"have inclusive scopes. Each link in the availability and visibility "
"definitions only checks the immediate predecessor, so intermediate "
"operations can bridge scope gaps that the endpoints cannot satisfy directly. "
"Such a chain passes through at least one availability operation and at least "
"one visibility operation with inclusive scopes, such that their common scope "
"includes both ``W`` and ``R``."
msgstr ""

